N5008 [temp.arg]/2 + [temp.deduct]/8: an explicit TYPE template argument
supplied to an overload whose first template parameter is a NON-TYPE
parameter (`get<double>(v)` against `get<size_t N>(V<Ts...>&)`) is a
deduction failure that removes that candidate only; the by-type overload
is selected.  Before, it was the hard error "expected expression, but got
type" (the mirror of the value-for-type case).
